<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea intervenes, selling dlrs in forward.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea intervenes, selling dlrs in forward.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea (BOK) intervened in the inter-bank foreign exchange market in early morning on Monday, by selling dollars in forward trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the central bank sold dollars at 907 won in three-month forward and at 917 won in six-month forward.</p>
</text>
